<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB sells 2,000 tonnes wheat at A$218/tonne.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB sells 2,000 tonnes wheat at A$218/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said bids were submitted for 26,000 tonnes of wheat and that 2,000 tonnes of Australian Hard 13 percent protein (AH13) wheat were sold at tender on Wednesday for A$218.00 a tonne, Fremantle delivery.</p>
<p>All bids were for new crop wheat, the AWB said.</p>
<p>The AWB said highest failed bids in A$ a tonne were:</p>
<p>    Port Zone	 Grade			Bids</p>
<p>    Newcastle	 ASW			  158.50</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide   AH13			 208.00</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide   AH1			  195.00</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide   SFT1			 187.00</p>
<p>    Fremantle	 GP1			  179.00</p>
<p>Closing date for the next tender is January 8, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - AH: Australian Hard.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
